      "writtenOn": "2017-02-21T09:05:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This test checks that when a callback is registers and gets AVAILABLE, the other callbacks follow, but it doesn\u0027t appear to check that the other callbacks follow if an AVAILABLE callback is sent to an *already-registered* callback object.\n\nWe should test that. Options I see for doing so are:\n\n1. Add a bit more code to this test that brings up a higher-\n   scoring network (e.g., validated wifi) and tests that\n   dfltNetworkCallback gets the capability and linkproperty\n   changed callbacks.\n2. Add a convenience method (expectAvailableCallbacks?) that\n   expects all three callbacks on a given network, and replace\n   all the calls to expectCallback(CallbackState.AVAILABLE)\n   with calls to this new method.\n3. Somehow modify TestNetworkCallback#expectCallback to\n   expect the other callbacks as well if the test code is\n   expecting AVAILABLE.\n\n#1 seems simplest but it\u0027s not great in terms of coverage. I\u0027d prefer #2 or #3.",
      "revId": "098554650a981618e7012fb44bdd4adcefe7ac60",
